# SALAH configuration
#
# SALAH is offline-first. Prayer times, Qibla, Hijri dates and the prayer log
# are computed on this device; the Quran is bundled. Two things use the network,
# both optional: verse audio, and one GET of the Ministry of Habous' monthly
# timetable when the device is online. With the radio off every screen works.
#
# There are no API keys, no server endpoints and no accounts, and no `.env` file
# is read at build time. Gradle reads the *process environment*; this file is a
# template for your shell.
#
# Release signing is the only thing that needs credentials, and those are read
# from the environment (never from a file in the repo):
#   KEYSTORE_PATH   path to the upload keystore (.jks)
#   STORE_PASSWORD  keystore password
#   KEY_ALIAS       key alias (default: upload)
#   KEY_PASSWORD    key password (default: STORE_PASSWORD)
#
# Source it before a release build:
#   set -a; . ./.env; set +a
#
# Without those variables a release task fails; it never falls back to the
# debug keystore, because a Play Store upload rejects a debug-signed build.
